---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/site';
---

<Layout
  title="The studio"
  description="Meet Alphpaca, an independent software studio and product company combining practical engineering with long-term product thinking."
>
  <section class="container page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">The studio / Independent by nature</span>
    <h1>
      We care about
      <br />
      <span class="gold-text">what we build.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="hero-description">
      And just as much about why we build it. Alphpaca brings product thinking
      and software engineering together to turn useful ideas into dependable
      digital products.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="container section split-story">
    <div class="studio-mark">
      <img
        src={url('alphpaca-emblem.svg')}
        width="260"
        height="270"
        alt="Alphpaca’s gold alpaca emblem"
      />
      <span class="eyebrow">Thoughtful software. Long-term thinking.</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">A studio with a builder’s mindset</span>
      <h2>
        Close to the problem.
        <br />
        Committed to the craft.
      </h2>
      <p>
        Good software is a series of good decisions. What to build. What to
        leave out. Where to keep things simple, and where to invest for the
        future.
      </p>
      <p>
        We work with founders and teams who want a hands-on technical partner.
        Our approach connects the needs of the business, the experience of the
        user, and the reality of maintaining a system after launch.
      </p>
      <p>
        We also build our own products. Atlas Cloud and Eduroo put that same
        approach to work in cloud infrastructure and education—two areas where
        better tools can make a real difference.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">What guides us</span>
        <h2>
          Principles we
          <br />
          put into practice.
        </h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="values-grid">
      <article>
        <span class="eyebrow">01 / Understand first</span>
        <h3>Start with the problem.</h3>
        <p>
          Talk to the people using the product. Define the outcome. Challenge
          assumptions before they become expensive features.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="eyebrow">02 / Build deliberately</span>
        <h3>Make complexity earn its place.</h3>
        <p>
          Choose tools that fit the job. Prefer readable code and clear
          architecture. Leave the system easier to understand than you found it.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="eyebrow">03 / Own the work</span>
        <h3>Stay accountable.</h3>
        <p>
          Make tradeoffs visible, share progress early, and raise the hard
          questions. A useful partnership depends on honest communication.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="eyebrow">04 / Think beyond launch</span>
        <h3>Build for the next chapter.</h3>
        <p>
          Consider accessibility, security, observability, and maintenance from
          the start. Shipping is a milestone, not the end of the story.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section manifesto">
    <span class="eyebrow">Our perspective on AI</span>
    <h2>
      Better tools.
      <br />
      <span class="gold-text">The same responsibility.</span>
    </h2>
    <p>
      AI-assisted development can shorten the path from an idea to a working
      product. We see it as a tool for exploration, implementation, and
      review—with engineers responsible for the architecture, validation, and
      final result.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our standard stays the same: understand what we ship, protect sensitive
      information, and verify the behavior that matters.
    </p>
  </section>
  <CTA />
</Layout>
